# === The @eigen family-root prism decl ===
#
# Per prism-as-trait-as-everything: `prism @eigen { ... }` declares
# @eigen IS a prism. Five-operation block below is the canonical
# declaration form (cf. boot/00-prism.mirror).

prism @eigen {
  focus eigen
  project eigen
  split eigen
  shift eigen
  settle eigen
}

# === @eigen(T) — the type-level Foerster COORD decorator ===
#
# The core operator. Produces a substrate view where `T`'s carrier
# admits the fixed-point discipline `Op(x) = x`.
#
# Substrate-decl semantics:
#
#   Given a landed value-type T with a recursion R: T → T:
#     @eigen(T) is the type-level projection that names the set of
#     fixed points {x ∈ T | R(x) = x}.
#     The witness IS the identity per Foerster 1976 + Kauffman 2003.
#
# Applied to landed value-types:
#
#   @eigen(crystal) — the settled crystal at fixed-point of
#                      settle-recursion.
#   @eigen(splinter) — the atom at fixed-point (trivial).
#   @eigen(Liquid<T>) — the excited-state carrier at fixed-point
#                        of the dH¹/dt ≤ 0 contraction.
#   @eigen(system_spec) — the VSM system-declaration at fixed-point
#                          of the mosaic.focus walk (per @mirror/spec/
#                          system canonical spec §2 obligation
#                          discharge).
#
# Composition-primitive naming per feedback_composition_primitive_
# naming_convention: `eigen(T) -> ref` reads as: given a type T,
# produce a substrate view (`ref`).
eigen(t: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === eigen_of_carrier — bilateral property predicate ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - the carrier `t` has an associated recursion R: T → T declared
#     (typically via `settle` op at the carrier's altitude)
#   - the witness `x` is a fixed point of R modulo bounded discrepancy
#     (per @eigen/form's is_fixed_point discharge; forward-promised
#     species-under-@eigen)
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (carrier reference
# non-null; witness reference non-null; fixed-point discharge
# delegated to @eigen/form species-decl at forward-promise altitude).
#
# Sentinel: `eigen=type-level-foerster-coord-fixed-point`.
bilateral eigen_of_carrier {
  sentinel "eigen=type-level-foerster-coord-fixed-point"
  arity 2
}
eigen_of_carrier(t: ref, x: ref) -> verdict { \ }

